(HALVERD INSTRUMENTS, INC.) Tj
T*
(Quarterly Report — Third Quarter, Fiscal Year 2026) Tj
T*
(Quarter ended 31 July 2026. Reported 20 August 2026.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SUMMARY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Revenue for the third quarter was $24.9 million, a decrease of 14 percent against the) Tj
T*
($29.0 million reported in the third quarter of fiscal 2025. Gross margin was 51.2 percent.) Tj
T*
(Operating loss was $2.6 million. Net loss was $2.1 million, or $0.12 per diluted share.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We are reducing full-year fiscal 2026 revenue guidance to $104 million to $109 million,) Tj
T*
(from the $118 million to $124 million range reaffirmed in our second-quarter report.) Tj
T*
(Full-year gross margin guidance is reduced to 53 to 55 percent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The reduction has two causes, both discussed below. The HX-9 depth drift defect is) Tj
T*
(materially larger than we estimated in the second quarter and now requires a partial) Tj
T*
(recall. Trondsen Offshore has deferred two survey programmes pending completion of that) Tj
T*
(work.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(One matter has resolved favourably: the second source for the PT-40 pressure transducer) Tj
T*
(die completed qualification during the quarter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Halverd Instruments is a fictional company. This document was written to demonstrate retrieval software and describes no real business, product, person or transaction.) Tj
T*
