(SEGMENT RESULTS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Subsea Sensing revenue was $13.1 million, down 31 percent year over year. The decline is) Tj
T*
(attributable almost entirely to deferred HX-9 and Vessel Integration Kit shipments to) Tj
T*
(Trondsen Offshore.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Industrial Calibration revenue was $11.8 million, flat against the prior quarter and up 1) Tj
T*
(percent year over year. The segment will finish fiscal 2026 below the range set in) Tj
T*
(November, as indicated in the second-quarter report.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Backlog at quarter end was $51.4 million. Backlog rose while revenue fell because deferred) Tj
T*
(Trondsen orders remain in backlog rather than being cancelled.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CUSTOMER CONCENTRATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Trondsen Offshore AS accounted for 29 percent of third-quarter revenue, down from 41) Tj
T*
(percent in the second quarter. The change reflects lower absolute shipments to Trondsen) Tj
T*
(rather than growth elsewhere. On 11 June 2026 Trondsen deferred two survey programmes,) Tj
T*
(together representing approximately $7.4 million of planned third and fourth quarter) Tj
T*
(revenue, until HX-9 remediation is complete and verified on their fleet. Trondsen has not) Tj
T*
(cancelled and has not sought damages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(No other customer accounted for more than 11 percent of revenue in the quarter.) Tj
T*
ET
