(HX-9 DEPTH DRIFT — REVISED ESTIMATE AND RECALL) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Field data collected after the second-quarter report changes both the scope and the cost) Tj
T*
(of this defect.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Onset is earlier than we reported. Drift begins at approximately 600 hours of continuous) Tj
T*
(submersion, not the 900 hours stated in the second-quarter report. The 900-hour figure) Tj
T*
(came from bench testing at constant temperature; the shorter onset appears in units cycled) Tj
T*
(through thermoclines, which is ordinary operating use.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The affected population is larger than we reported. Firmware 4.1.3, which we had excluded,) Tj
T*
(carries the same accumulator defect. The affected population is therefore 7,450 units) Tj
T*
(rather than the 3,100 units stated in the second-quarter report.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Approximately 1,200 of those units are on hardware revision B, which cannot accept) Tj
T*
(firmware 4.4.2 over the vessel link. Those units must be returned and reflashed at a) Tj
T*
(service centre. We announced this partial recall on 3 July 2026.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The warranty accrual recorded in the second quarter was $2.4 million, and we stated at the) Tj
T*
(time that we believed it sufficient. It is not sufficient. We have increased the total) Tj
T*
(accrual to $6.1 million, recording an additional $3.7 million charge in the third quarter.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
