(LIQUIDITY, CAPITAL AND OUTLOOK) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cash and cash equivalents were $38.2 million at 31 July 2026, against $44.6 million at the) Tj
T*
(end of the second quarter. The company carries no debt. The reduction is principally the) Tj
T*
(third-quarter operating loss, $2.9 million of cash warranty spend, and $1.4 million of) Tj
T*
(capital expenditure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(REVISED FULL-YEAR GUIDANCE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Revenue guidance for fiscal 2026 is reduced to $104 million to $109 million, from $118) Tj
T*
(million to $124 million. Of the approximately $14 million reduction at the midpoint, we) Tj
T*
(attribute roughly $7.4 million to the deferred Trondsen programmes and the remainder to) Tj
T*
(slower HX-9 shipments generally while the recall is in progress.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The revised guidance assumes that the total warranty accrual of $6.1 million is sufficient,) Tj
T*
(that the recall completes during the fourth quarter, and that Trondsen resumes deliveries) Tj
T*
(in the first quarter of fiscal 2027. We note that our previous sufficiency estimate for) Tj
T*
(this defect proved wrong by a factor of more than two.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
